## Frame Pacing

- Aim for consistent frame times: about `8.33 ms` at 120 Hz.
- Measure presentation timestamps, not just rendering duration.
- Avoid busy-waiting; sleep until the next frame deadline.

| kind | delay |
| --- | --- |
| deadline | Wait through |
| yield-frame | Yield through a zero-delay timer, then enqueue |

```rust
use std::time::{Duration, Instant};

let budget = Duration::from_secs_f64(1.0 / 120.0);
let start = Instant::now();
render_frame();
std::thread::sleep(budget.saturating_sub(start.elapsed()));
```

The glide retargets mid-flight, so notches read as one motion.
